WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.363 --> 00:00:02.584
- Any kind of art discipline,

00:00:02.584 --> 00:00:04.295
I think the possibilities are endless.

00:00:04.295 --> 00:00:08.617
I think this life is so
brief and we spend it,

00:00:08.617 --> 00:00:13.254
sometimes, imposing over
ourselves, so many limitations.

00:00:13.254 --> 00:00:17.451
Never underestimate a five
foot three Columbian girl.

00:00:17.451 --> 00:00:18.572
- Shakira is a firecracker.

00:00:18.572 --> 00:00:19.547
- Whee.

00:00:19.547 --> 00:00:21.285
- She's a Columbian singer, songwriter,

00:00:21.285 --> 00:00:22.913
dancer, and record producer.

00:00:22.913 --> 00:00:24.628
Her song "Hips Don't Lie" is one of the

00:00:24.628 --> 00:00:27.822
best selling singles of the 21st century.

00:00:27.822 --> 00:00:29.653
She has a star on the
Hollywood Walk of Fame

00:00:29.653 --> 00:00:32.677
and is one of the best selling
Latin artists of all time.

00:00:32.677 --> 00:00:34.456
She's Shakira, and here's my take on

00:00:34.456 --> 00:00:36.259
her top ten rules for success.

00:00:36.259 --> 00:00:37.918
Rule number one is my personal favorite,

00:00:37.918 --> 00:00:40.077
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:40.077 --> 00:00:41.111
Also guys, as you're watching

00:00:41.111 --> 00:00:41.999
if you hear something that really

00:00:41.999 --> 00:00:43.647
resonates with you, please leave it

00:00:43.647 --> 00:00:44.816
down in the comments below

00:00:44.816 --> 00:00:47.528
and put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired.

00:00:47.528 --> 00:00:49.598
Also, when you write it
down, it's much more likely

00:00:49.598 --> 00:00:52.943
to lock in for yourself as well, enjoy.

00:00:52.943 --> 00:00:55.619
(wind gust)

00:00:55.619 --> 00:00:58.202
(lively music)

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:07.134
- I grew up in Columbia.

00:01:07.134 --> 00:01:10.395
And Columbia, it's a developing country

00:01:10.395 --> 00:01:14.067
where a lot of people don't have access

00:01:14.067 --> 00:01:16.019
to the most basic needs

00:01:16.019 --> 00:01:19.183
and where education is
considered a luxury,

00:01:19.183 --> 00:01:20.794
unfortunately, because we all know that

00:01:20.794 --> 00:01:22.961
education is a birthright.

00:01:25.172 --> 00:01:27.503
I just grew up frustrated seeing

00:01:27.503 --> 00:01:30.086
how many people weren't able to

00:01:32.436 --> 00:01:34.612
realize their own dreams, you know.

00:01:34.612 --> 00:01:36.199
When I was eight years old,

00:01:36.199 --> 00:01:40.140
my dad underwent an economic
crisis, a financial crisis,

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:42.905
he lost his business, and we struggled,

00:01:42.905 --> 00:01:45.616
economically, for many years.

00:01:45.616 --> 00:01:46.949
We lost our car,

00:01:48.352 --> 00:01:51.285
we lost our furniture, (laughs)

00:01:51.285 --> 00:01:53.509
and I remember vividly the day I walked in

00:01:53.509 --> 00:01:55.032
my house and all the furniture was gone

00:01:55.032 --> 00:01:58.048
because my dad had to pay his debts.

00:01:58.048 --> 00:02:01.381
And it was quite, well, shocking for me.

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:04.730
I was seven, eight years old,

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:06.290
and when I saw this

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:07.652
I was so frustrated.

00:02:07.652 --> 00:02:09.239
I was so upset with my parents cause

00:02:09.239 --> 00:02:12.030
I couldn't understand
how they did so poorly

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:13.111
in business, you know?

00:02:13.111 --> 00:02:16.361
I'm like "Why, why?" I couldn't get it.

00:02:17.519 --> 00:02:19.962
My dad and my mom took me to the park

00:02:19.962 --> 00:02:21.697
where they showed me other kids,

00:02:21.697 --> 00:02:23.579
my age, sniffing glue.

00:02:23.579 --> 00:02:24.469
They were orphans.

00:02:24.469 --> 00:02:27.904
They had no one to watch after them.

00:02:27.904 --> 00:02:31.437
They were barefoot and they were abandoned

00:02:31.437 --> 00:02:32.943
to their own luck.

00:02:32.943 --> 00:02:36.819
And it, probably, left such an impression

00:02:36.819 --> 00:02:40.147
in my impressionable mind, at that age,

00:02:40.147 --> 00:02:42.493
that I remember that day.

00:02:42.493 --> 00:02:45.826
I remember that I made myself a promise.

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:50.121
I said to myself Shakira,
you have to succeed,

00:02:50.121 --> 00:02:51.704
because you have to

00:02:53.999 --> 00:02:57.412
ride in a car again one day, (laughs)

00:02:57.412 --> 00:03:01.087
you have to get your own car someday.

00:03:01.087 --> 00:03:03.328
I wanted to vindicate my parents,

00:03:03.328 --> 00:03:06.460
socially and economically,
and I also wanted

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:08.581
to someday do something for those kids

00:03:08.581 --> 00:03:10.277
who I saw that day in the park.

00:03:10.277 --> 00:03:13.576
So, as soon as I had my
first big success with

00:03:13.576 --> 00:03:17.635
Pies Descalzos, which was my third album,

00:03:17.635 --> 00:03:19.335
I decided to establish my own foundation

00:03:19.335 --> 00:03:23.196
and do my own contribution to the change.

00:03:23.196 --> 00:03:25.321
Even if it was going to be a small one.

00:03:25.321 --> 00:03:27.822
But I wanted to be active.

00:03:27.822 --> 00:03:29.320
And that's how it all started.

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:32.373
Going through my own financial struggle

00:03:32.373 --> 00:03:34.187
and the struggle of my family

00:03:34.187 --> 00:03:36.464
and understanding that the one thing

00:03:36.464 --> 00:03:39.797
that I never lacked was care, protection

00:03:41.218 --> 00:03:42.446
and an education.

00:03:42.446 --> 00:03:45.249
And that's, probably, what
made me thrive in life.

00:03:45.249 --> 00:03:49.009
I didn't know exactly how this
album was going to turn out.

00:03:49.009 --> 00:03:51.393
You can never predict
those kind of things.

00:03:51.393 --> 00:03:53.055
There's nothing scarier than standing

00:03:53.055 --> 00:03:55.066
in front of a white canvas.

00:03:55.066 --> 00:03:56.433
You never know if you're going to be able

00:03:56.433 --> 00:04:00.433
to provide something new
to those who expect it.

00:04:01.718 --> 00:04:04.551
But in any kind of art discipline,

00:04:05.709 --> 00:04:09.458
I think the possibilities are endless.

00:04:09.458 --> 00:04:12.618
That's something that I
always learn the hard way,

00:04:12.618 --> 00:04:14.604
with every album, because I suffer

00:04:14.604 --> 00:04:15.512
through the process sometimes.

00:04:15.512 --> 00:04:17.649
I'm like, oh my God, I'm never going to do

00:04:17.649 --> 00:04:19.272
anything that I like.

00:04:19.272 --> 00:04:22.105
Until boom, it appears, magically.

00:04:24.545 --> 00:04:27.248
I guess, if you keep rubbing the lamp

00:04:27.248 --> 00:04:31.038
the genies of the lamp has
got to show up at sometime.

00:04:31.038 --> 00:04:33.455
This has been my experience
throughout the years.

00:04:33.455 --> 00:04:37.945
With every album, I get
really, really nervous

00:04:37.945 --> 00:04:40.528
the first months in the studio.

00:04:41.791 --> 00:04:42.624
Searching,

00:04:43.947 --> 00:04:45.142
exploring,

00:04:45.142 --> 00:04:49.272
trying things that sometimes don't work,

00:04:49.272 --> 00:04:51.583
until you find the magic,

00:04:51.583 --> 00:04:52.933
or the magic finds you

00:04:52.933 --> 00:04:55.419
while you're working. (laughs)

00:04:55.419 --> 00:04:57.644
- So when you meet new
talent, emerging talent

00:04:57.644 --> 00:04:59.811
and you're mentoring them,

00:05:00.822 --> 00:05:02.801
what if you don't have a confidence

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:04.559
that they have the level of talent

00:05:04.559 --> 00:05:06.136
required to achieve greatness?

00:05:06.136 --> 00:05:07.784
How do you counsel them?

00:05:07.784 --> 00:05:11.915
What do you say to make
them feel confident

00:05:11.915 --> 00:05:14.605
to not rob them of that
moment but also steer them

00:05:14.605 --> 00:05:16.274
in the right direction?

00:05:16.274 --> 00:05:19.690
I mean, you can't say,
really, "You're a zero."

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:20.611
(laughter)

00:05:20.611 --> 00:05:21.605
- By talking to them,

00:05:21.605 --> 00:05:24.049
understanding what their concerns are,

00:05:24.049 --> 00:05:26.882
what sort of self-image they have,

00:05:27.941 --> 00:05:31.691
and trying to show them
their strengths, too.

00:05:33.034 --> 00:05:34.560
If they have some kind of weakness,

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:38.143
we'll try to not focus
on those weaknesses.

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:44.137
I think in entertainment
industry that's what works.

00:05:45.247 --> 00:05:48.330
You know your strengths, you milk em.

00:05:49.291 --> 00:05:50.818
You know your weaknesses, you try not

00:05:50.818 --> 00:05:52.430
to focus on them so much,

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:55.650
so the audience doesn't
focus on them as much.

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:59.244
I'm more worried now about being true

00:05:59.244 --> 00:06:01.847
to myself and being honest.

00:06:01.847 --> 00:06:02.855
Maybe ten years ago,

00:06:02.855 --> 00:06:05.694
I would have not done a
video like, "She Wolf"

00:06:05.694 --> 00:06:09.112
but now, it's something I feel like doing.

00:06:09.112 --> 00:06:11.326
So why am I going to deprive myself

00:06:11.326 --> 00:06:15.493
or deny myself the possibility
of expressing the way I feel?

00:06:18.265 --> 00:06:19.933
I want to express myself freely.

00:06:19.933 --> 00:06:23.379
I don't want to be in
a golden cage anymore.

00:06:23.379 --> 00:06:26.129
I don't want to be put behind bars.

00:06:27.883 --> 00:06:30.300
I think this life is so brief

00:06:31.406 --> 00:06:34.820
and we spend it, sometimes,
imposing over ourselves,

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:37.570
so many limitations and obstacles

00:06:38.537 --> 00:06:43.314
that don't allow us to
grow as we would like to.

00:06:43.314 --> 00:06:45.647
And yes, I feel like a woman

00:06:46.676 --> 00:06:49.019
and this time around I
wanted to show my legs.

00:06:49.019 --> 00:06:53.687
I never showed my legs
for 20 years. (laughs)

00:06:53.687 --> 00:06:57.687
I always did all my
performances with long pants

00:06:58.816 --> 00:06:59.724
believe it or not.

00:06:59.724 --> 00:07:01.356
I never showed my legs, and one day

00:07:01.356 --> 00:07:02.960
I looked and them and I
said "Hey, they're not bad."

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:05.561
"They're kind of short but
they take me to places."

00:07:05.561 --> 00:07:09.090
"I think it's now or never." (laughs)

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:12.253
It's about time to really embrace

00:07:12.253 --> 00:07:14.698
my individuality and my freedom

00:07:14.698 --> 00:07:16.163
as a woman, as a person.

00:07:16.163 --> 00:07:20.246
That's a message that I
encourage to other women.

00:07:21.254 --> 00:07:22.288
That doesn't mean, necessarily,

00:07:22.288 --> 00:07:23.900
letting yourself be objectified.

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:27.493
Because that means satisfying
the desires of other people.

00:07:27.493 --> 00:07:30.181
I say, satisfy your own desires,

00:07:30.181 --> 00:07:33.792
and live your life to the
fullest, because it's short.

00:07:33.792 --> 00:07:36.589
- All these awards, after
winning so many Grammys

00:07:36.589 --> 00:07:38.422
and the rest of it, what sort of motivates

00:07:38.422 --> 00:07:40.790
you to create new things, new music?

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:41.623
(sighs)

00:07:41.623 --> 00:07:43.570
- You know, I shouldn't be this motivated

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:46.425
because after so many years I should be

00:07:46.425 --> 00:07:47.904
a little bit more calm about everything.

00:07:47.904 --> 00:07:51.175
But I love what I do and I'm always

00:07:51.175 --> 00:07:53.051
putting myself in front of new challenges

00:07:53.051 --> 00:07:55.928
and I guess I'm still hungry.

00:07:55.928 --> 00:07:59.174
How am I going to discover the talent

00:07:59.174 --> 00:08:00.693
that my son has?

00:08:00.693 --> 00:08:03.377
How am I going to encourage him

00:08:03.377 --> 00:08:05.460
to follow his own dreams?

00:08:06.695 --> 00:08:09.725
It's a conundrum, and it's a challenge

00:08:09.725 --> 00:08:11.746
for every parent out there, I think.

00:08:11.746 --> 00:08:14.413
But if it weren't because of my mom,

00:08:14.413 --> 00:08:16.630
I think that I would have never made it,

00:08:16.630 --> 00:08:18.748
Cause she realized that I was talented,

00:08:18.748 --> 00:08:19.581
but not only that.

00:08:19.581 --> 00:08:22.966
She supported me, she believed in me

00:08:22.966 --> 00:08:25.549
and she went ahead and help me,

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:31.803
help me build my confidence,
my own confidence.

00:08:31.803 --> 00:08:34.886
Confidence in myself which is a vital

00:08:38.329 --> 00:08:42.496
tool that you need in order
to survive any kind of job.

00:08:44.264 --> 00:08:48.411
- Why do you think it all
came together for you?

00:08:48.411 --> 00:08:49.669
- Why?

00:08:49.669 --> 00:08:52.340
A lot of hard work, a
lot of determination.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:55.757
I consider myself a laborer of what I do.

00:08:56.674 --> 00:08:59.924
An artisan, and I think I've been

00:08:59.924 --> 00:09:03.924
building my career, putting
a brick over a brick

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:08.527
under the sun, with sweat and hard work.

00:09:08.527 --> 00:09:10.278
That's the way I've done it.

00:09:10.278 --> 00:09:13.866
I haven't given up, not one moment.

00:09:13.866 --> 00:09:15.674
There must be something very abnormal

00:09:15.674 --> 00:09:18.046
about this, because
it's been so many years

00:09:18.046 --> 00:09:21.046
doing this and I still care so much.

00:09:22.399 --> 00:09:23.504
I don't think that's normal.

00:09:23.504 --> 00:09:26.393
But with every project I feel

00:09:26.393 --> 00:09:27.226
that I haven't accomplished anything.

00:09:27.226 --> 00:09:29.892
That I feel that I'm starting from zero,

00:09:29.892 --> 00:09:32.374
and I care tremendously.

00:09:32.374 --> 00:09:34.620
In a way that, sometimes, it surprises me.

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:35.775
- So you feel like you have to
- It's still there.

00:09:35.775 --> 00:09:38.379
prove yourself over and over again.

00:09:38.379 --> 00:09:41.129
- Yes. I think that I have to be,

00:09:42.590 --> 00:09:46.757
that I have to embrace new
challenges and those challenges

00:09:49.737 --> 00:09:53.505
make me grow, and growing
is the only way to go.

00:09:53.505 --> 00:09:56.276
The only way I conceive life.

00:09:56.276 --> 00:09:59.545
So, yeah, that's the way I see it.

00:09:59.545 --> 00:10:01.099
I think that we all come to

00:10:01.099 --> 00:10:03.373
this world with a star, with a talent,

00:10:03.373 --> 00:10:04.513
and with a gift.

00:10:04.513 --> 00:10:07.263
And then, later, dreams are born.

00:10:08.231 --> 00:10:09.653
And no one, absolutely no one

00:10:09.653 --> 00:10:13.028
has the authority to stop those dreams.

00:10:13.028 --> 00:10:14.540
When I was seven years old,

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:16.391
I came to Los Angeles for the first time

00:10:16.391 --> 00:10:18.677
and I passed by the Walk of Fame

00:10:18.677 --> 00:10:20.791
with my mother and a friend
of hers who's, actually,

00:10:20.791 --> 00:10:22.344
here with us today, (laughs)

00:10:22.344 --> 00:10:24.571
(crowd cheers)

00:10:24.571 --> 00:10:27.923
and I remember that my mom
told me, "Shaki, one day you're

00:10:27.923 --> 00:10:30.257
"going to have your name on this place."

00:10:30.257 --> 00:10:32.888
(cheering)

00:10:32.888 --> 00:10:34.671
If someone would have
overheard this conversation

00:10:34.671 --> 00:10:37.485
they would have thought
that my mom was delirious.

00:10:37.485 --> 00:10:40.829
But she was not, and here we are.

00:10:40.829 --> 00:10:43.092
so I want to say to all of you

00:10:43.092 --> 00:10:45.646
to dream as big as you can,

00:10:45.646 --> 00:10:49.496
because in this country
everything is possible.

00:10:49.496 --> 00:10:51.353
- You sound so passionate about so many

00:10:51.353 --> 00:10:54.026
diverse pieces of your life,

00:10:54.026 --> 00:10:57.013
that the big question is
how do you juggle all that?

00:10:57.013 --> 00:10:59.871
How do you make all of that
happen and successfully?

00:10:59.871 --> 00:11:02.596
From your music career, to being a mom,

00:11:02.596 --> 00:11:04.888
to being a life partner, like all of that

00:11:04.888 --> 00:11:06.937
is so hard to juggle.

00:11:06.937 --> 00:11:07.770
How do you do it?

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:10.270
What's the secret behind that?

00:11:11.404 --> 00:11:13.556
- I don't know how I'm going
to keep doing it. (laughs)

00:11:13.556 --> 00:11:16.817
That's a good question,
because with a baby

00:11:16.817 --> 00:11:18.701
things tend to change a lot.

00:11:18.701 --> 00:11:20.828
But I have a great team,

00:11:20.828 --> 00:11:25.761
people who understand me very
well, who understand my cause,

00:11:25.761 --> 00:11:29.021
my commitments and who support em

00:11:29.021 --> 00:11:30.968
and make my life easier.

00:11:30.968 --> 00:11:33.523
So it is very important
to be well surrounded.

00:11:33.523 --> 00:11:35.636
- You're perfect, Shakira. You're perfect.

00:11:35.636 --> 00:11:37.197
(crowd cheers)

00:11:37.197 --> 00:11:38.438
- She is the perfect woman.

00:11:38.438 --> 00:11:39.271
But you're talking about winning

00:11:39.271 --> 00:11:40.462
this show right now.

00:11:40.462 --> 00:11:41.547
- C'mon!

00:11:41.547 --> 00:11:42.646
- Don't be mean!

00:11:42.646 --> 00:11:43.479
- Uh oh!

00:11:43.479 --> 00:11:44.973
(crowd cheers)

00:11:44.973 --> 00:11:45.806
- Dammit.

00:11:45.806 --> 00:11:46.993
(laughs)

00:11:46.993 --> 00:11:49.981
There is nothing worse than being scolded

00:11:49.981 --> 00:11:53.895
by Shakira when she goes from zero to 100

00:11:53.895 --> 00:11:56.845
and you're not going to get a word in.

00:11:56.845 --> 00:11:58.903
- I'm speaking to you
- Hey, you know what--

00:11:58.903 --> 00:11:59.941
from the bottom of my heart.
- And you know what--

00:11:59.941 --> 00:12:02.879
how things are going to
get on this competition.

00:12:02.879 --> 00:12:03.891
- And with the--
- Sorry.

00:12:03.891 --> 00:12:04.724
(crowd laughs)

00:12:04.724 --> 00:12:05.557
- Baa.

00:12:05.557 --> 00:12:06.683
- You never get into an argument

00:12:06.683 --> 00:12:07.764
with a Latin woman.

00:12:07.764 --> 00:12:09.134
Oh, no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:12:09.134 --> 00:12:10.173
You don't mess with Shakira.

00:12:10.173 --> 00:12:11.154
Don't debate with her.

00:12:11.154 --> 00:12:13.079
- I'll take that--
- Hold on, time out, time out.

00:12:13.079 --> 00:12:13.912
- Are you sure?
- Time out.

00:12:13.912 --> 00:12:15.438
It's a complicated decision.
- Time out.

00:12:15.438 --> 00:12:17.201
- While she's talking, shut up.

00:12:17.201 --> 00:12:18.249
- I just want to say something.

00:12:18.249 --> 00:12:19.523
- Aba-a.

00:12:19.523 --> 00:12:22.939
- You guys, you are a completely
different animal, you know?

00:12:22.939 --> 00:12:24.413
(crowd laughs)

00:12:24.413 --> 00:12:25.493
These are alpha dogs.

00:12:25.493 --> 00:12:27.154
Perros alfa.

00:12:27.154 --> 00:12:28.308
(laughter)

00:12:28.308 --> 00:12:32.326
Never underestimate a five
foot three Colombian girl.

00:12:32.326 --> 00:12:33.567
- Shakira is a firecracker.

00:12:33.567 --> 00:12:34.400
- Waa.

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:36.129
- She's very spicy.

00:12:36.129 --> 00:12:36.962
- You're coming to my team,

00:12:36.962 --> 00:12:38.727
so let's make this quick.
- Ah, ah, ah, ah, ah, ah, ah.

00:12:38.727 --> 00:12:40.285
Not without my permission first.

00:12:40.285 --> 00:12:41.391
- Here's what I do when Shakira starts

00:12:41.391 --> 00:12:42.861
getting feisty, I do this.

00:12:42.861 --> 00:12:46.182
(lively music)

00:12:46.182 --> 00:12:48.262
- I, Shakira Mebarak,

00:12:48.262 --> 00:12:50.393
born in Barranquilla, Columbia,

00:12:50.393 --> 00:12:52.103
- I promise you, I, Adam Levine

00:12:52.103 --> 00:12:53.075
from Los Angeles, California.

00:12:53.075 --> 00:12:55.910
(laughter)

00:12:55.910 --> 00:12:56.910
- Hey, Adam.

00:12:58.649 --> 00:13:00.771
You know, he has this tattoo that says

00:13:00.771 --> 00:13:02.246
"Wrong coach for you."

00:13:02.246 --> 00:13:03.833
(laughter)

00:13:03.833 --> 00:13:05.267
- Damn. The claws are out.

00:13:05.267 --> 00:13:06.562
(cat screech)

00:13:06.562 --> 00:13:07.395
- It's hard.

00:13:07.395 --> 00:13:08.832
It's hard to be right all the time.

00:13:08.832 --> 00:13:09.847
Ah, ah, no, no, no.

00:13:09.847 --> 00:13:11.208
- That's, that's not, but that--

00:13:11.208 --> 00:13:12.386
- Are you going to take that?

00:13:12.386 --> 00:13:13.219
- Hey.

00:13:13.219 --> 00:13:14.296
(crowd laughs)

00:13:14.296 --> 00:13:16.518
Hey, my hips don't lie.

00:13:16.518 --> 00:13:17.916
I don't lie either.

00:13:17.916 --> 00:13:19.940
- Tell him Shakira, tell him.

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:21.850
(laughter)

00:13:21.850 --> 00:13:23.126
- Personally, I think it's adorable.

00:13:23.126 --> 00:13:25.158
I actually love that side of her.

00:13:25.158 --> 00:13:27.577
- It doesn't matter what
Shakira says, it's always right.

00:13:27.577 --> 00:13:28.543
- Thank you.

00:13:28.543 --> 00:13:31.126
(crowd cheers)

00:13:32.843 --> 00:13:34.204
- Thank you guys so much for watching

00:13:34.204 --> 00:13:36.958
I made this video because
Khalid Azzam asked me to.

00:13:36.958 --> 00:13:38.017
So, if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:13:38.017 --> 00:13:39.718
that you want me to profile next

00:13:39.718 --> 00:13:40.794
leave it down in the comments below

00:13:40.794 --> 00:13:41.975
and I'll see what I can do.

00:13:41.975 --> 00:13:43.939
I'd also love to know what did Shakira say

00:13:43.939 --> 00:13:45.569
that had the biggest impact on you?

00:13:45.569 --> 00:13:48.100
What clip was your
favorite from these ten?

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:49.688
And also, what are you
going to immediately

00:13:49.688 --> 00:13:51.644
take from this video and apply somehow

00:13:51.644 --> 00:13:53.214
to your life or to your business?

00:13:53.214 --> 00:13:54.932
Leave it down in the comments below

00:13:54.932 --> 00:13:56.631
and I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:13:56.631 --> 00:13:57.797
Finally, I want to give a quick shout out

00:13:57.797 --> 00:13:59.914
to Damn Purvis. Damn, thank you so much

00:13:59.914 --> 00:14:01.213
for picking up a copy of my book

00:14:01.213 --> 00:14:03.123
"Your One Word", it
really, really, really,

00:14:03.123 --> 00:14:04.470
really means a lot to me and I hope

00:14:04.470 --> 00:14:05.584
you're enjoying the read.

00:14:05.584 --> 00:14:07.076
So thank you guys so much for watching

00:14:07.076 --> 00:14:08.277
I believe in you.

00:14:08.277 --> 00:14:10.221
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:14:10.221 --> 00:14:13.497
and whatever your one word is, much love.

00:14:13.497 --> 00:14:15.547
I'll see you soon.

00:14:15.547 --> 00:14:17.964
(wind whips)

00:14:20.749 --> 00:14:22.630
- To be able to succeed in America

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:24.115
was very important.

00:14:24.115 --> 00:14:27.361
It represented to me a
reaffirmation, as an artist.

00:14:27.361 --> 00:14:29.947
He should keep it, just
have notes, you know?

00:14:29.947 --> 00:14:31.388
Let's try it.

00:14:31.388 --> 00:14:34.280
Performing at the VMAs means freedom.

00:14:34.280 --> 00:14:36.809
It means that you really have your chance

00:14:36.809 --> 00:14:38.782
to do whatever you want up on stage.

00:14:38.782 --> 00:14:40.749
And it means being among

00:14:40.749 --> 00:14:42.683
the most successful artists.

00:14:42.683 --> 00:14:43.858
It's too long still.

00:14:43.858 --> 00:14:46.025
(singing)

00:14:48.092 --> 00:14:50.655
If I could just conquer
my own insecurities

00:14:50.655 --> 00:14:53.155
and conquer other hearts, too,

00:14:54.986 --> 00:14:57.333
it would demonstrate that my music

00:14:57.333 --> 00:14:59.421
was powerful enough to transcend

00:14:59.421 --> 00:15:00.372
so many barriers.

00:15:00.372 --> 00:15:02.781
Da, da, da, da, da, da, boom.

00:15:02.781 --> 00:15:04.152
- Ga, ga, ga, ga, ga, ga, boom.

00:15:04.152 --> 00:15:05.304
- Yeah. There.

00:15:05.304 --> 00:15:08.554
(singing and clapping)

00:15:10.458 --> 00:15:12.216
You do one, then you wait.

00:15:12.216 --> 00:15:13.236
- [Male Voice] No, no, that's it.

00:15:13.236 --> 00:15:14.848
- And then you. (laughs)

00:15:14.848 --> 00:15:16.993
You know, I'm so excited
with what we have now,

00:15:16.993 --> 00:15:19.636
that I would like the
VMAs to happen tonight.

00:15:19.636 --> 00:15:20.877
I would be ready.

00:15:20.877 --> 00:15:23.479
♫ I'm falling apart in your hands again

00:15:23.479 --> 00:15:27.229
I am the conqueror. (laughs)

